{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain4j/langchain4j/pulls/6584","id":4739749685,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJx3NCM8AAAABGoLXNQ","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain4j/langchain4j/pull/6584","diff_url":"https://github.com/langchain4j/langchain4j/pull/6584.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/langchain4j/langchain4j/pull/6584.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain4j/langchain4j/issues/6584","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain4j/langchain4j/pulls/6584/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain4j/langchain4j/pulls/6584/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain4j/langchain4j/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain4j/langchain4j/issues/6584/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain4j/langchain4j/statuses/6356c3e6e3da3b717f24d19920be074b7061fc0e","number":6584,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(mcp): propagate async tool cancellation","user":{"login":"mumuzi6","id":151131799,"node_id":"U_kgDOCQIWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151131799?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mumuzi6","html_url":"https://github.com/mumuzi6","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mumuzi6/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mumuzi6/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mumuzi6/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mumuzi6/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mumuzi6/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mumuzi6/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mumuzi6/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mumuzi6/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mumuzi6/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"\r\n## Issue\r\n\r\nFixes #6583\r\n\r\n## Change\r\n\r\n`DefaultMcpClient.executeToolAsync()` returned a dependent `CompletableFuture` without propagating caller cancellation back to the underlying MCP request.\r\n\r\nCancelling the caller-facing future now:\r\n\r\n- cancels the in-flight MCP response future;\r\n- sends `notifications/cancelled` when required by the existing transport/protocol semantics;\r\n- does not send that notification for transports where it is unnecessary;\r\n- preserves the existing timeout behavior.\r\n\r\n`CancellationException` is also preserved as cancellation instead of being treated as an ordinary tool execution error. This matches the blocking `executeTool()`, which already surfaces a cancellation (for example a `notifications/cancelled` sent by the server) as a `CancellationException`, as `executeToolAsync()`'s Javadoc says it should. Cancellation is reported to `McpClientListener.onExecuteToolError` while preserving `CancellationException` instead of wrapping it in `ToolExecutionException`.\r\n\r\nNote for callers of `executeToolAsync()`: a request cancelled by the server now fails with `CancellationException` (as with `executeTool()`) instead of `ToolExecutionException`.\r\n\r\nRegression tests cover:\r\n\r\n- caller cancellation propagating to the underlying request;\r\n- the returned future remaining in the cancelled state;\r\n- a cancellation notification with the correct request ID and `\"Cancelled\"` reason when required;\r\n- no cancellation notification for modern HTTP;\r\n- a server-side cancellation surfacing as `CancellationException`;\r\n- listener error notification for both caller-side and server-side cancellation, including exactly-once behavior when cancellation paths race.\r\n\r\n## General checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] There are no breaking changes (API, behaviour)\r\n- [X] I have added unit and/or integration tests for my change\r\n- [X] The tests cover both positive and negative cases\r\n- [ ] I have manually run all the unit and integration tests in the module I have added/changed, and they are all green\r\n- [ ] I have manually run all the unit and integration tests in the [core](https://github.com/langchain4j/langchain4j/tree/main/langchain4j-core) and [main](https://github.com/langchain4j/langchain4j/tree/main/langchain4j) modules, and they are all green\r\n- [ ] I have added/updated the [documentation](https://github.com/langchain4j/langchain4j/tree/main/docs/docs)\r\n- [ ] I have added an example in the [examples repo](https://github.com/langchain4j/langchain4j-examples) (only for \"big\" features)\r\n- [ ] I have added/updated [Spring Boot starter(s)](https://github.com/langchain4j/langchain4j-spring) (if applicable)\r\n\r\nThe module unit tests are green; the module integration suite and the core/main suites were not run locally. Documentation, examples, and Spring Boot starter changes are not applicable to this scoped MCP cancellation fix.\r\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-05T03:18:50Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T13:00:24Z","closed_at":"2026-10-06T13:00:10Z","merged_at":"2026-10-06T13:00:09Z","merge_commit_sha":"3913c09a59f5a9430d108d111a9acc4d3921ff52","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"mumuzi6:fix-mcp-async-cancellation","ref":"fix-mcp-async-cancellation","repo":{"id":1405045252,"node_id":"R_kgDOU79KBA","name":"langchain4j","full_name":"mumuzi6/langchain4j","owner":{"login":"mumuzi6","id":151131799,"node_id":"U_kgDOCQIWlw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151131799?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mumuzi6","html_url":"https://github.com/mumuzi6","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mumuzi6/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mumuzi6/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mumuzi6/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mumuzi6/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mu